{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/804280-the-fool-s-luck-podcast-episode","id":804280,"title":"The Fool's Luck [podcast episode]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-08T23:49:15-08:00","id":804280,"title":"The Fool's Luck [podcast episode]","content":"From: <a href=\"http://midnightexpress.podbean.com/e/episode-20-the-fools-luck-readers-companion/\" target=\"_blank\">http://midnightexpress.podbean.com/e...ers-companion/</a><br /> <br /> The hosts continue in the spirit of the Changeling 20 Kickstarter by devoting an episode to The Fool's Luck: The Way of the Commoner. The book is reviewed in detail and the hosts dwell on a few of their favourite societies, Treasures, and themes from the book.<br /> Join us next month for a discussion on cross-over games with Dark Alliance: Vancouver. In the meantime, drop by the forum, the Facebook page or send us an email.<br /> <br /> Hosts: BK, Wendell_Burke, and Darling_Rose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T03:11:14-08:00","id":804312,"title":"","content":"Nice.<br /> <br /> On the subject of the sidhe: I always find it interesting when republicans (or people from a republic) defend them, while I (someone from a constitutional monarchy) absolutely think the tone of The Fool's Luck is correct. Shouldn't I be the one who wants to play the nobility? Incontrovertible proof that I'm a contrarian, I guess. :-P <br /> <br /> I mean, the sidhe just came back and stole land, right? There's little sympathy to be had.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 01-09-2016, 06:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T03:51:07-08:00","id":804328,"title":"","content":"I live in a republican nation too, but I love the sidhes and monarchy (in games). That's because only those who never lived in a monarchy and are unaware of their problems can see anything interesting on it, I think. Hahaha","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5821-neon-sidhe","name":"Neon.Sidhe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5821_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T08:08:13-08:00","id":804459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neon.Sidhe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/804280-the-fool-s-luck-podcast-episode?p=804328#post804328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I live in a republican nation too, but I love the sidhes and monarchy (in games). That's because only those who never lived in a monarchy and are unaware of their problems can see anything interesting on it, I think. Hahaha</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're right. Of course, there is also a kind of heroic romanticism to a feudal society, and I think most people want to believe in their leaders, because the alternative is, well, depressing.<br /> <br /> The truth of Changeling is more complex: the Dreaming gives the sidhe certain Birthrights which make it easier for them to rule, but these Birthrights often seem to rely on convincing others of their right to rule, rather than giving sufficient practical evidence of such.<br /> <br /> There's a darker analogue to the sidhe, still: that of Imperialism and conquer. European nations invaded ('settled') other countries on the pretext that they were a) bringing civilisation (in other words, their own rules) and b) that they were best suited to ruling (under the terms, of course, that they themselves were importing).<br /> <br /> This is much like the sidhe. They arrive and claim the right to rule because, well, their rules say so. Never mind the rules of the commoners who've been doing just fine without them for centuries.<br /> <br /> This can all be balanced, though, when you consider that the commoners, too, once stole land from the Nunnehi, and are still contesting certain magical sites with Garou, mages, humans, etc. And before them, the Tuatha came and stole the lands of the Fomorians, who possibly stole theirs (depending on which myths you read) from the fir-bholg.<br /> <br /> The sidhe are just the latest villains in a long saga of villainy and conquest. I still don't like them, though... ;-)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T09:44:52-08:00","id":804509,"title":"","content":"I like villains and anti-hero characters, maybe that's why I like the sidhes so much. :-)<br /> <br /> Actually, there's some things that bothers me about commoners. I think they (the setting designers) tried too hard to put them as &quot;the good guys&quot; sometimes, like that story about dual souls (I completely ignore it as a house rule) and all that hate against nobles from other denizens of the dreaming completely ignoring the rest of the kithain, like they know all about kithain and can blame a kith and not the others for something they've done...<br /> I like commoners (don't get me wrong), but sometimes I think it's interesting make them more complex and explore more shades of grey.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5821-neon-sidhe","name":"Neon.Sidhe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5821_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T11:34:09-08:00","id":804573,"title":"","content":"The twin souls thing is interesting, although I got bored of it on principle by the time we got to Mummy: The Resurrection, where it seemed just about everybody was either a human soul and something else, or just another creature in a human body.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T11:07:51-08:00","id":809719,"title":"","content":"I don't know, I do enjoy the sidhe as both heroes and villains. they are after all, just as much people as any changeling and often have their own views and ideals. Personally, I'd like to see a more balanced approach to the narrative that gives as much emphasis to the good the sidhe have done for the dreaming and the commoners as much as their crimes of conquest. for example, it could be argued that the sidhe legitimately brought a form of structure and peace to some lands that were more often plagued by never ending wars between feuding commoners. or how they could discover or reclaim freeholds and trods thought lost for centuries after the shattering allowing more glamour into the world and pushing back the endless winter. Emphasis that there is a just and fair ruler love by their subjects for every imperialistic villain out there. ( it might sound like a fairy tale but remember that in the dreaming those have a habit of becoming literal reality.) in other words, make the sidhe just as interesting and dynamic as the other kiths in terms of the fluff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5767-deedee","name":"DeeDee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T05:42:58-08:00","id":810190,"title":"","content":"I think all the kiths suffer from Second Edition-itis. Splats were much more uniform then than in the Revised Era. Take, for instance, the write up of the pooka, which seems to pretty much demand you play a lying trickster. Most of them were written with similarly narrow descriptions. I think there's much less breadth in those descriptions than, say, Mage Traditions or even Vampire clans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}